WEBVTT

00:05.846 --> 00:09.808
I'll be able to reconvene with
Melone in about an hour.

00:10.059 --> 00:13.604
Ghiaccio, I'm gonna leave this job
to you and Melone.

00:14.146 --> 00:15.939
Like I say, better safe than sorry.

00:16.065 --> 00:20.444
I'll work to piece together
the clues back here.

00:20.569 --> 00:22.445
<i>Got it, Risotto.</i>

00:23.906 --> 00:26.617
How long's this gonna take?
Step on it.

00:26.659 --> 00:29.036
You should be able to reconstruct
this thing, no problem.

00:31.080 --> 00:32.372
Risotto.

00:32.873 --> 00:34.332
You do know
there will be repercussions

00:34.416 --> 00:36.126
for going against Passione, right?

00:36.710 --> 00:38.628
You're lucky I'm short on time.

00:44.677 --> 00:46.345
Your left eye will be next.

00:46.929 --> 00:49.389
Remember, all you need is your
right arm and eye to do your job.

00:49.431 --> 00:51.808
You should know better than anyone!

00:51.976 --> 00:53.644
The boss will make any and all
traitors disappear

00:53.686 --> 00:55.145
from the face of the earth…

01:09.785 --> 01:14.285
<i>Heavy stones of fate
are holding down my dreams</i>

01:15.124 --> 01:18.585
<i>It feels as if I'm being crushed</i>

01:20.337 --> 01:24.837
<i>I've been staggering around
with nowhere to hide</i>

01:25.509 --> 01:29.346
<i>But I will never give in</i>

01:29.430 --> 01:33.930
<i>I know there are fragments of hope
buried beneath all that rubble</i>

01:41.191 --> 01:45.691
<i>I will find them with my own hands
and turn this world upside down</i>

01:54.288 --> 01:58.788
<i>Fighting gold
We will shine one day</i>

02:00.252 --> 02:04.752
<i>As long as we continue to
believe in our own path</i>

02:07.343 --> 02:10.471
<i>We are unyielding souls</i>

02:10.512 --> 02:15.012
<i>Our battle against god
will keep raging on</i>

02:15.768 --> 02:20.268
<i>Until our final days
Fighting gold</i>

02:29.698 --> 02:34.077
EPISODE 18
VERSO VENEZIA!

02:30.532 --> 02:31.533
What?!

02:31.742 --> 02:34.099
That hand is already
a living, breathing thing,

02:36.038 --> 02:37.748
and it's devouring you
from the inside out.

02:39.875 --> 02:42.085
As you can see, it's a piranha!

02:51.136 --> 02:55.056
Wow, it totally ripped him open
from stem to stern…

02:55.182 --> 02:56.725
How can he still be moving?

02:58.227 --> 03:00.812
W-What's wrong, Babyhead?

03:00.896 --> 03:02.272
Answer me! Hey!

03:02.398 --> 03:03.524
THIS IS TURTLE SHIT…

03:04.400 --> 03:07.194
That turtle's dirty shit
is now all over my face!

03:07.236 --> 03:10.656
I don't deserve this kind of
torture and humiliation…

03:10.906 --> 03:12.490
Damn it!

03:12.866 --> 03:14.951
This psychological trauma…

03:15.536 --> 03:17.454
You're gonna pay dearly for this…

03:18.497 --> 03:20.624
You're gonna die
like a pathetic dog

03:20.666 --> 03:21.958
in a shit pool of shame!

03:22.459 --> 03:26.959
If I have to take you out
to heal Bucciarati and Trish…

03:28.590 --> 03:29.882
then that is what I'll do!

03:30.384 --> 03:31.510
Your luck's run out…

03:31.593 --> 03:33.553
Next time, I'll aim
for that ugly head!

03:33.804 --> 03:35.388
Eat your heart out…

03:36.265 --> 03:37.975
you test a di cazzo!

03:38.058 --> 03:39.809
DICKHEAD
I'll KILL YOU…
EAT YOUR HEART OUT…

03:40.769 --> 03:41.978
Oh shit…

03:42.062 --> 03:43.646
Remote tracking is great

03:43.689 --> 03:46.358
when that little bastard
decides to follow orders.

03:48.402 --> 03:49.569
Idiot!

03:50.738 --> 03:52.823
You know I've been attacked
by you three times now.

03:53.365 --> 03:55.158
I've got you
pretty figured out now!

04:02.166 --> 04:04.376
That bastard's range…

04:05.085 --> 04:06.628
got a lot longer!

04:12.217 --> 04:13.843
My baby's growing up…

04:14.136 --> 04:16.388
So he loses his temper
and has a growth spurt!

04:16.472 --> 04:17.764
Di motto!

04:17.931 --> 04:19.599
I knew that salty shrew
would turn out to be

04:19.641 --> 04:20.933
the most amazing mom!

04:23.812 --> 04:25.522
Simple is best.

04:25.731 --> 04:29.860
I'm gonna snuff out this coglione
the way I want to!

04:30.360 --> 04:32.403
Reverse course, Golden Wind!

04:32.529 --> 04:33.863
Die!

04:37.284 --> 04:38.285
Muda!

04:40.329 --> 04:41.330
Bullseye.

04:44.875 --> 04:46.334
Open your eyes.

04:46.627 --> 04:48.962
I think that's called a whiff!

04:49.463 --> 04:52.507
I win. Now to kill you!

04:53.008 --> 04:55.093
You do know what muda means, yes?

04:59.515 --> 05:01.391
W-What the hell?!

05:01.642 --> 05:02.934
Open your eyes.

05:03.018 --> 05:07.397
Golden Wind wasn't playing fetch
with his own hand.

05:08.732 --> 05:09.733
That was the bike.

05:10.359 --> 05:11.943
I transformed the bike
into a living hand

05:12.027 --> 05:13.570
and had the new life form
delivered here.

05:17.074 --> 05:21.036
You just assimilated that machine
into your body.

05:21.703 --> 05:22.829
Excellent work.

05:22.955 --> 05:24.998
You and your third rate tricks…
You can't defeat me…

05:25.040 --> 05:28.209
I'll just split apart
and get away aga—

05:28.252 --> 05:29.419
You're forgetting.

05:29.461 --> 05:31.421
Motorcycles have
tanks of gas to run.

05:32.506 --> 05:35.091
So it wouldn't be difficult for me
to ignite you

05:35.175 --> 05:37.594
before you could even contemplate
splitting and running away.

05:38.428 --> 05:40.221
What?!

05:49.273 --> 05:52.734
I'm on fire… The pain…

05:53.360 --> 05:56.905
Guess doing things your way…

05:57.406 --> 05:58.407
didn't work out for ya.

05:59.408 --> 06:01.326
BURN BURN BURN BURN
BURN BURN BURN… ING…!

06:01.785 --> 06:03.453
He… He's gone?

06:03.704 --> 06:05.122
I've lost all contact?!

06:05.205 --> 06:07.290
Dammit, I don't believe this!

06:07.416 --> 06:08.625
Damn that freshman!

06:14.506 --> 06:15.507
He did it.

06:27.519 --> 06:29.312
It's gotta be around here
somewhere…

06:29.938 --> 06:33.316
- Someone had the gall to take my car!
- Where's my car? Was it stolen?!

06:34.192 --> 06:36.819
That's Melone's bike…

06:36.987 --> 06:39.739
The only way to catch
those bastards, they said…

06:39.781 --> 06:43.326
is to leave no stone unturned
and think outside the box…

06:43.577 --> 06:45.704
I get "leave no stone unturned."

06:45.787 --> 06:47.455
Any idiot gets that.

06:47.831 --> 06:51.000
I mean, who doesn't turn over rocks
to find stuff from time to time.

06:51.877 --> 06:55.463
But what does "think outside
the box" even mean?!

06:55.505 --> 06:57.173
Maybe I think clearer inside a box!

06:57.215 --> 06:58.341
Merda!

06:58.383 --> 06:59.759
That's the dumbest!

06:59.801 --> 07:02.136
So my skull's a freakin' box now?!

07:02.179 --> 07:04.347
You think I'm
some kind of idiot, cazzo!

07:06.475 --> 07:08.727
<i>Hey, Melone! Bucciarati
and his accomplices</i>

07:08.810 --> 07:10.269
<i>are completely gone!</i>

07:11.813 --> 07:14.232
<i>Are you listening?! Pronto?!</i>

07:14.316 --> 07:15.525
I hear you all right…

07:15.943 --> 07:18.028
Don't go assuming
I'm down-and-out just yet, stronzo!

07:19.029 --> 07:21.489
I've still got
Bucciarati's precious lifeblood!

07:21.573 --> 07:23.866
Mass producing Juniors
is a piece of cake!

07:24.785 --> 07:26.870
They'll hunt him down
Iickety split!

07:28.163 --> 07:30.290
I sure do hope so, my Melone.

07:30.582 --> 07:32.709
The new guy is dangerous.

07:32.793 --> 07:34.753
We have to dispose of him first.

07:36.588 --> 07:39.173
I'll find a truly wicked surrogate

07:40.092 --> 07:43.386
who'll birth a powerful
and vicious beast.

07:45.222 --> 07:48.141
A new beast starving for blood.

07:50.602 --> 07:52.395
What the hell was that?

07:53.230 --> 07:54.773
It looked like a snake…

07:55.065 --> 07:56.858
<i>What? What's wrong?</i>

07:56.900 --> 07:59.235
Why the hell is there a snake
in Roma Termini?

08:04.199 --> 08:05.575
I-It's burning!

08:06.159 --> 08:09.203
So this is what
that annoying newbie can do…

08:09.246 --> 08:11.373
He must've used Junior's corpse to—

08:18.630 --> 08:19.756
<i>Pronto?</i>

08:20.132 --> 08:23.135
<i>Hey, Melone!
What's wrong? Hey!</i>

08:26.054 --> 08:28.598
The venomous snake I left
at Roma Termini

08:28.682 --> 08:30.934
is back to being
a worthless hunk of evil.

08:30.976 --> 08:32.644
The user is now dead.

08:32.728 --> 08:33.812
That makes five.

08:34.187 --> 08:35.938
If what we know so far is correct,

08:35.981 --> 08:38.775
the Hitman Team has only
two surviving members left.

08:39.026 --> 08:40.902
We can't rest on our laurels.

08:41.278 --> 08:43.321
Let's hightail it to Venezia,
pronto, boys!

08:45.615 --> 08:47.575
They got Melone too?

08:48.744 --> 08:51.079
Merda, merda, merda!

08:51.121 --> 08:52.497
Merda!

08:54.583 --> 08:55.667
<i>Pronto?!</i>

08:56.209 --> 08:59.170
It's me. I've analyzed the hell
out of you know what.

08:59.254 --> 09:00.255
<i>Huh?!</i>

09:00.464 --> 09:02.382
I'm sending my findings over now.

09:11.308 --> 09:13.351
We've got a new directive
from the boss.

09:14.352 --> 09:15.353
Abbacchio,

09:15.437 --> 09:17.480
I'd like you to come here
and take a look at something.

09:17.814 --> 09:18.815
Me?

09:20.525 --> 09:21.734
This is the message.

09:22.027 --> 09:25.321
Beside the chair, Abbacchio is to
activate Moody Jazz

09:25.405 --> 09:27.990
and rewind time
by more than fourteen hours.

09:28.033 --> 09:32.370
Someone was here before us.

09:32.579 --> 09:33.871
Or that's the implication.

09:34.164 --> 09:35.165
Right, let's go.

09:35.624 --> 09:38.043
Let's see where fifteen hours
takes us.

09:45.133 --> 09:46.342
We've got form.

09:48.011 --> 09:50.680
Hey, haven't we seen
this old guy before!

09:50.764 --> 09:52.348
It's signore Pericolo, the capo.

09:52.474 --> 09:54.309
So he was the one
who placed the turtle

09:54.351 --> 09:57.020
by the drinking fountain
at Napoli Centrale.

09:57.270 --> 09:59.230
And about fourteen hours ago,

09:59.314 --> 10:01.107
he was standing
right where we are now.

10:01.817 --> 10:03.026
I'll resume playback.

10:04.361 --> 10:06.529
<i>Ragazzi, listen and listen well…</i>

10:07.072 --> 10:09.449
<i>I'm about to convey to
your final mission.</i>

10:10.325 --> 10:11.326
Final mission?

10:11.660 --> 10:14.037
<i>Strict confidentiality requires me</i>

10:14.121 --> 10:16.540
<i>to adopt this mode
of communication.</i>

10:16.998 --> 10:18.874
<i>Under no circumstances
should you share</i>

10:18.917 --> 10:20.835
<i>any of the following information.</i>

10:20.877 --> 10:22.712
<i>For you will learn
the specific process</i>

10:22.754 --> 10:24.380
<i>by which you are to
deliver Trish to the boss.</i>

10:25.132 --> 10:26.216
Specific process…

10:26.299 --> 10:27.383
Deliver Trish?

10:28.468 --> 10:29.886
<i>Now for the crux.</i>

10:29.970 --> 10:32.097
<i>Up on your arrival in Venezia,</i>

10:32.347 --> 10:34.474
<i>you are to proceed
to this sculpture,</i>

10:34.516 --> 10:37.685
<i>inside which you will
obtain the OA-DISC.</i>

10:37.936 --> 10:40.146
<i>It contains information
that details the specifics</i>

10:40.188 --> 10:42.190
<i>concerning the location
of the handover.</i>

10:43.358 --> 10:44.734
Hey! What's he…?!

10:44.818 --> 10:46.402
Abbacchio, pause it!

10:46.736 --> 10:47.737
Right.

10:49.447 --> 10:52.116
Of course, this is the gateway
to the city of water…

10:52.534 --> 10:54.244
It's Santa Lucia Station.

10:54.703 --> 10:56.121
That's our lion statue.

10:57.539 --> 10:58.665
<i>That is all.</i>

10:58.707 --> 11:01.543
<i>You must obtain the OA-DISC.</i>

11:01.585 --> 11:04.129
<i>But know they are well aware
of my influence.</i>

11:04.337 --> 11:08.257
<i>The how in safely delivering Trish
to her father</i>

11:08.300 --> 11:10.927
<i>is absolutely critical.</i>

11:10.969 --> 11:13.346
<i>You must not leave a single piece
of evidence behind</i>

11:14.097 --> 11:18.226
<i>The boss blessed me with
a full and fulfilling life,</i>

11:18.268 --> 11:21.396
<i>replete with experiences
most can only dream of</i>

11:22.022 --> 11:24.107
<i>Ragazzi,
my mission is now complete.</i>

11:26.151 --> 11:28.111
<i>From the deepest depths of
my mafia soul,</i>

11:28.195 --> 11:29.446
<i>I pray for all your safety.</i>

11:34.326 --> 11:37.078
Oh my God!

11:45.086 --> 11:46.420
Mr. Pericolo…

11:56.056 --> 11:58.641
I suppose they have received
the directive now.

12:03.313 --> 12:05.481
You must obtain the disc.

12:05.523 --> 12:08.776
Without it, our meeting will be met
with extreme difficulty.

12:09.778 --> 12:12.322
In the final moment,
all will be decided…

12:12.906 --> 12:15.783
You must bring my daughter,
my Trish, to me…

12:18.620 --> 12:20.496
…at Venezia.

12:29.464 --> 12:32.300
<i>Floating in the ethereal dawn,
a city of baroque grandeur awaits…</i>

12:32.342 --> 12:33.343
<i>Venezia.</i>

12:33.802 --> 12:36.471
<i>Only one road connects
the Italian mainland</i>

12:36.513 --> 12:38.264
<i>with the historical island center.</i>

12:38.306 --> 12:40.808
<i>The over three-kilometers long
Ponte della Libertà</i>

12:40.850 --> 12:43.018
<i>straddles the shallow
Venetian lagoon.</i>

12:43.561 --> 12:45.938
<i>Beyond it, almost instantly,
lies the stazione.</i>

12:45.981 --> 12:47.524
<i>There, by the facade,
the team will find</i>

12:47.607 --> 12:50.026
<i>their fated Venetian lion
and its mysterious prize.</i>

12:55.073 --> 12:58.409
Giorno, looks like
we're clear so far.

12:58.535 --> 13:00.912
Yeah, all looks clear up front too.

13:01.204 --> 13:02.747
The city is still slumbering.

13:03.123 --> 13:05.166
We're the only ones on the road.

13:05.750 --> 13:08.085
Why do these windows
keep fogging up so fast?

13:10.338 --> 13:11.380
Ow!

13:13.341 --> 13:14.717
What the hell?!

13:14.801 --> 13:16.052
Sorry about that.

13:16.094 --> 13:18.054
Guess the tires are skidding a bit.

13:18.096 --> 13:20.306
On a road as straight as an arrow?

13:20.348 --> 13:23.225
Well, pay attention, dufus.
Do you even have a license?

13:23.351 --> 13:25.311
Why would I? I'm fifteen.

13:28.982 --> 13:32.568
What the hell's stuck
on the window?

13:32.694 --> 13:34.570
Guess the thing's on the inside.

13:34.654 --> 13:37.573
I was focusing too much out there
to notice…

13:38.366 --> 13:39.909
No, wait…

13:40.327 --> 13:41.619
That thing looks like a…

13:42.329 --> 13:43.830
finger!

13:49.085 --> 13:50.878
Let's crack the windows a bit then.

13:51.046 --> 13:53.131
The difference in temperature
from in here to out there

13:53.214 --> 13:54.465
is causing the condensation.

13:55.216 --> 13:57.760
W-What?! What's with this wind?

13:59.429 --> 14:03.141
You know, it really sent
a chill down my spine… But…

14:03.558 --> 14:06.769
Once we performed a little
computer analysis on those ashes,

14:06.853 --> 14:09.522
piecing together that photo
Pericolo burned

14:09.564 --> 14:10.815
was really pretty easy.

14:11.232 --> 14:12.608
What a dumb move!

14:13.443 --> 14:16.696
You grade A idiot as can't escape
the Hitman Team!

14:16.738 --> 14:19.866
An enemy?! How the hell
did they get on the roof!

14:20.075 --> 14:21.659
Mista, what are you doing?!

14:21.743 --> 14:23.536
Start shooting and turn this
into a convertible!

14:23.578 --> 14:27.248
Shit, it's like this car
is being cryogenically frozen.

14:27.290 --> 14:29.333
It's so freakin' cold,
you can't even feel it.

14:29.417 --> 14:31.502
My finger clean ripped off

14:31.586 --> 14:33.462
and is now a frozen fish stick
on the window

14:33.546 --> 14:34.630
and I didn't even notice.

14:35.590 --> 14:37.508
If I don't peel my face off,

14:37.592 --> 14:39.594
this thing the freeze is gonna
creep into my brain.

14:39.594 --> 14:42.305
Then again, do I really wanna
live with half a face…

14:43.973 --> 14:45.432
Where's the turtle?

14:45.475 --> 14:46.642
I don't know about you,

14:46.726 --> 14:47.977
but I don't see
a reptile anywhere in here.

14:48.269 --> 14:51.814
You two aren't with
Trish and Bucciarati?

14:51.898 --> 14:54.567
It must be a pretty big deal
that you're going it alone…

14:55.110 --> 14:56.444
I got it!

14:56.736 --> 15:00.698
Your assignment must be to pick up
something really important then.

15:00.782 --> 15:02.158
The place in the picture…

15:02.242 --> 15:04.410
Something's at Santa Lucia!

15:05.787 --> 15:08.080
<i>Finally, I'm actually bleeding!</i>

15:11.251 --> 15:13.044
- Yeehaw!
- Yeehaw!

15:12.627 --> 15:14.295
BONK

15:15.713 --> 15:17.589
I-Ice!

15:18.091 --> 15:21.219
He covered himself in ice and
stuck himself to the damn roof!

15:21.302 --> 15:24.179
The bullets are getting stuck
before getting him!

15:25.140 --> 15:26.099
What's wrong?

15:26.141 --> 15:29.269
Shit, guys, we're starting
to freeze too!

15:30.353 --> 15:32.188
Do something! Help!

15:32.272 --> 15:33.481
Number Two!

15:33.523 --> 15:34.565
Don't go!

15:35.984 --> 15:38.528
- Number Two! Number Three!
- Number Two! Number Three!

15:39.696 --> 15:40.863
What?!

15:43.408 --> 15:45.034
A-All I did was blink…

15:45.076 --> 15:48.037
And now, my eyelashes
are stuck together!

15:49.664 --> 15:50.706
He planned all this

15:50.748 --> 15:52.207
and waited for the exact moment
to jump on the roof…

15:52.500 --> 15:55.920
We're traveling at eighty
kilometers an hour now.

15:56.212 --> 15:57.504
Which means…

15:57.672 --> 15:58.923
The wind is blowing around us

15:59.007 --> 16:00.758
at the equivalent of
twenty kilometers a second.

16:01.176 --> 16:03.386
The wind chill factor
drops one degree Celsius

16:03.470 --> 16:05.638
for every meter of wind speed,

16:05.972 --> 16:09.517
so we're freezing to death
at minus twenty degrees Celsius.

16:09.559 --> 16:11.060
Then stop the damn car!

16:11.186 --> 16:13.771
When the hell were you
planning on breaking?!

16:14.105 --> 16:16.315
Well, funny you should
mention that.

16:16.566 --> 16:17.608
Thing is…

16:17.692 --> 16:20.069
the damn break is frozen solid
and it won't go down!

16:20.320 --> 16:21.571
The steering wheel's gone, too.

16:21.613 --> 16:23.072
The engine's still humming,

16:23.156 --> 16:24.490
so it doesn't look to be
stopping anytime soon.

16:28.244 --> 16:32.164
The car's exterior has dropped
to minus one hundred!

16:32.415 --> 16:34.208
It works at such incredible speed…

16:34.250 --> 16:36.085
This has got to be
the enemy's Stand!

16:38.213 --> 16:42.592
Th-The blood from my severed finger
is hard as a rock now…

16:44.052 --> 16:47.805
The moisture from my breath is
making my nostrils freeze over…

16:49.390 --> 16:50.808
It's happening to my lips too…

16:50.850 --> 16:52.351
Shit! I can't breathe!

16:52.894 --> 16:54.437
S-Stop the car, Giorno!

16:54.562 --> 16:56.814
Turn it into a freakin' frog
or something!

16:56.898 --> 16:58.941
I don't care how you do it,
just do something!

16:59.067 --> 17:01.319
I've already tried that
a long time ago.

17:01.402 --> 17:05.614
No organism can survive at
negative hundred degrees Celsius!

17:09.827 --> 17:14.327
Everyone knows the capital
of France is Paris in English,

17:14.415 --> 17:15.624
and still the rest of the world

17:15.667 --> 17:17.293
pronounces it the authentic way
without the S.

17:17.919 --> 17:20.046
But for some crazy reason,
the English Venice

17:20.088 --> 17:22.131
pushed out the real Venezia
as the global standard.

17:22.382 --> 17:26.094
Like <i>The Merchant of Venice</i>
and <i>Death in Venice…</i>

17:26.761 --> 17:27.845
Perche cazzo?!

17:27.929 --> 17:31.515
Call the damn book
<i>Death in Venezia?!</i>

17:31.641 --> 17:33.225
What're we not good 'nuff?!

17:33.268 --> 17:34.310
Learn a little Italian

17:34.352 --> 17:36.145
and call it the way
it's supposed to be called!

17:36.187 --> 17:38.772
Freakin' pompous bullshit!

17:38.898 --> 17:40.441
Teste di merda!

17:45.446 --> 17:48.365
Looks like the cold is finally
starting to affect your driving.

17:48.491 --> 17:49.492
Mista…

17:49.784 --> 17:53.120
Golden Wind
requires warmth to work.

17:53.788 --> 17:55.414
I'm really sorry,

17:55.456 --> 17:57.499
there's just not much
I can do at this point…

17:57.792 --> 18:00.419
Picking up bullets is about it.

18:01.254 --> 18:02.546
I think you've reached your limit

18:02.630 --> 18:04.882
as far as blowing holes
in this car goes.

18:04.966 --> 18:07.134
I'll just put your body
into an even deeper free—

18:14.642 --> 18:17.645
Don't bullets retain
a little heat after being fired?

18:17.729 --> 18:21.357
So if I fire off those bullets
Giorno picked up for me…

18:21.399 --> 18:22.483
Then I'm packing heat.

18:22.525 --> 18:25.110
Well, since Giorno is
at a loss for words,

18:25.153 --> 18:27.196
I'll do him this one favor…

18:27.905 --> 18:30.032
Golden Wind!

18:37.498 --> 18:38.749
Successo!

18:38.875 --> 18:40.793
They don't look like much,

18:40.835 --> 18:45.335
but those little plant roots can
tear up asphalt and split boulders!

18:45.840 --> 18:47.174
Hold onto the wheel, Giorno!

18:47.216 --> 18:48.967
I think it's time to andiamo!

18:58.102 --> 18:58.894
Tch.

18:58.978 --> 19:02.564
Just as Melone said, the newbie
must've pulled this stunt.

19:02.607 --> 19:04.525
You don't get off that easy!

19:08.738 --> 19:10.406
Seriously? Stronzo!

19:10.490 --> 19:12.366
He's after us again!

19:12.408 --> 19:13.492
They better grab their tissues

19:13.534 --> 19:15.577
'cause Ghiaccio's
gonna go to the station

19:15.620 --> 19:16.912
and walk home with the goods.

19:19.374 --> 19:21.167
You're wasting your bullets.

19:21.209 --> 19:24.754
White Ice is very good at freezing
the moisture in the air

19:24.837 --> 19:26.463
at extremely low temperatures

19:26.547 --> 19:28.549
to make my very own
shimmering armor.

19:30.218 --> 19:32.220
It's great for skating
on almost any surface,

19:32.261 --> 19:34.554
and it's pretty darn good
at stopping

19:34.597 --> 19:37.099
pesky speeding bullets like yours!

19:37.725 --> 19:39.184
Go faster, Giorno!

19:39.268 --> 19:40.769
This thing can't go any faster!

19:40.770 --> 19:42.521
The tires are still slipping.

19:42.563 --> 19:45.566
Besides, they know all about
what's waiting at the station!

19:45.608 --> 19:47.276
Sure, they know that,
but they still don't have a clue

19:47.318 --> 19:48.944
as to where Trish
and the turtle are,

19:49.028 --> 19:50.571
which, if you ask me,

19:50.613 --> 19:52.489
is a pretty damn good
silver lining.

19:52.657 --> 19:55.493
You always come through
with your optimism.

19:55.576 --> 19:56.785
They're aren't many people
like you.

19:57.120 --> 19:58.955
He's here.
Come on, step on it!

19:59.038 --> 20:00.289
I told you, I can't!

20:00.373 --> 20:02.792
We'll lose speed
if we start sliding agai—

20:02.834 --> 20:05.378
I don't care… Step on the damn gas,
for the last time!

20:05.420 --> 20:07.630
I told you,
you're wasting your time!

20:07.797 --> 20:10.841
Number Three and Number Two,
get off the roof and get back here!

20:16.973 --> 20:20.977
Hope you enjoy long, hot
make-out sessions with asphalt.

20:21.018 --> 20:23.895
You and the road are about to
get real physical, real fast.

20:28.359 --> 20:29.610
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

20:29.986 --> 20:31.737
Good, we lost the freakazoid.

20:31.779 --> 20:34.740
Now let's get going.
The station's just ahead!

20:37.702 --> 20:41.956
We can still grab the goods and
hide before he catches up to us!

20:42.582 --> 20:43.583
Giorno!

20:45.293 --> 20:47.169
Keep dreaming!

20:47.211 --> 20:51.590
I'll make sure you guys never
make it to the stazione!

20:51.674 --> 20:54.093
He's freezing the moisture
from the car's exhaust!

20:54.135 --> 20:57.346
How cold does it have to be
for that shit to freeze?

20:57.680 --> 21:00.808
Bastard…
Here's another dose of hot lead!

21:02.477 --> 21:04.687
He opened the trunk!
Which means…

21:07.190 --> 21:10.902
Sh-Shit! Unwanted cargo!
Stop the car, Giorno!

21:10.985 --> 21:14.113
He's gonna try freezing
the breaks again!

21:14.363 --> 21:16.573
You should stop wasting
your breath…

21:16.616 --> 21:18.576
Gun-fondling Mista.

21:19.494 --> 21:21.287
Seeing that Trish
is nowhere to be seen.

21:21.329 --> 21:24.582
I can now do
what I came here to do.

21:25.500 --> 21:26.834
Shatter—

21:35.134 --> 21:36.135
G-Giorno!

21:38.346 --> 21:39.722
<i>It only cracked?</i>

21:40.181 --> 21:41.724
<i>Does this stronzo die?</i>

21:42.183 --> 21:44.268
<i>How do I dissolve his armor…?</i>

21:44.727 --> 21:46.937
Giorno! Get away from him!

21:47.104 --> 21:48.897
No! Not yet!

21:55.863 --> 21:57.406
We've made it to Venezia!

21:57.657 --> 21:59.075
Make room 'cause I'm diving in!

23:38.466 --> 23:42.052
EPISODE 19
WHITE ICE
